#. TRANSLATORS: "Flesch Reading Ease" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:824
msgid ""
"Amstad is a recalculation of Flesch Reading Ease for German text. It is "
"meant for secondary and adult-level text. Scores range from 0-100 (the "
"higher the score, the easier to read). Average documents should be within "
"the range of 60-70."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:860
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#schwartz\">Schwartz German Readability Graph</a> is "
"designed for classroom instructional materials."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:882
msgid ""
"This test is meant for secondary-age non-fiction (specifically, 6-10 "
"grade materials)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:906 projects/base_project.cpp:929
msgid ""
"This test is meant for primary-age non-fiction (specifically, light "
"materials up to the 5th grade)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:951
msgid ""
"German variation of Wheeler-Smith, which is meant for primary-age reading "
"materials."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:972
msgid "Rix (German fiction)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:973
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Rix meant for German fiction (specifically, "
"grades 1-11)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:999
msgid "Rix (German non-fiction)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1000
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Rix meant for German non-fiction "
"(specifically, secondary-age to adult level materials)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1020 projects/base_project.cpp:1021
msgid "Lix (German children's literature)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1022
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Lix meant for German children's literature "
"(specifically, grades 1-8). A <a href=\"#german-lix-gauge\">chart</a> is "
"also available to visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1044
msgid "Lix (German technical literature)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1045
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Lix meant for German technical/non-fiction "
"literature. A <a href=\"#german-lix-gauge\">chart</a> is also available "
"to visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1068
msgid ""
"Qu is generally appropriate for secondary age (4th grade to college "
"level) readers."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1085
msgid ""
"A German adaption of SMOG, which is generally appropriate for secondary "
"age (4th grade to college level) readers. SMOG tests for 100% "
"comprehension, whereas most formulas test for around 50%-75% "
"comprehension."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1120
msgid ""
"SOL is meant for secondary-age (4th grade to college level) Spanish "
"reading materials. It is a modified version of SMOG that was recalibrated "
"for Spanish text."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1151
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#gilliam-pena-mountain-graph\">Gilliam-Peña-Mountain graph</"
"a> is designed for most text, including literature and technical "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1182
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#frase-graph\">FRASE graph</a> is designed for educational "
"materials (primarily Spanish as a secondary language)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1206
msgid ""
"The Crawford test is designed for primary-age Spanish reading materials. "
"A <a href=\"#crawford-graph\">chart</a> is also available to visualize "
"the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1228
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#inflesz\">INFLESZ Scale</a> is a Flesch Reading Ease like "
"graph for Spanish. It is designed as a general purpose formula for most "
"text."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1266
msgid ""
"Harris-Jacobson is generally used for primary and secondary age "
"(Kindergarten to 11th grade) readers."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1291
msgid ""
"Spache is generally used for primary age (Kindergarten to 7th grade) "
"readers to help classify school textbooks and literature."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "New Dale-Chall" should not be translated; it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1313
msgid ""
"New Dale-Chall is generally used for primary and secondary age readers to "
"help classify school text books and literature."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1337
msgid ""
"PSK Dale-Chall is generally used for primary and secondary age readers to "
"help classify school text books and literature."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1359
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#fry-graph\">Fry graph</a> is designed for most text, "
"including literature and technical documents."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1390
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#raygor-graph\">Raygor estimate graph</a> is designed for "
"most text, including literature and technical documents."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Degrees of Reading Power" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1425
msgid ""
"Degrees of Reading Power is designed for matching documents to a "
"student's reading ability (based on his/her DRP score). This test is "
"influenced by sentence length, word length, and number of familiar Dale-"
"Chall words."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Degrees of Reading Power" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1450
msgid ""
"Degrees of Reading Power (GE) is designed for matching documents to a "
"student's reading ability (based on his/her DRP score). This test is a "
"conversion of a DRP (difficulty) score into a grade level."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Bormuth Grade Placement" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1473
msgid ""
"Bormuth Grade Placement is designed for students and is highly regarded "
"for its accuracy because it uses three variables (rather than the "
"traditional two variables)."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Bormuth Cloze Mean" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1496
msgid ""
"Bormuth Cloze Mean is designed for students and is highly regarded for "
"its accuracy because it uses three variables (rather than the traditional "
"two variables)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1518
msgid ""
"Wheeler-Smith is meant for primary-age (Kindergarten to 4th grade) "
"reading materials."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Automated Readability Index" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1541
msgid ""
"Automated Readability Index, also known as \"ARI\" or \"auto\", was "
"originally created for U.S. Air Force materials and was designed for "
"technical documents and manuals."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1564
msgid ""
"ELF is designed for \"listenability\" and is meant for radio and "
"television broadcasts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Gunning Fog" should not be translated; it is a test name
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1582
msgid ""
"Gunning Fog is generally recommended for business publications and "
"journals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "PSK Gunning Fog" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1616
msgid ""
"PSK Gunning Fog is generally recommended for business publications and "
"journals."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1634
msgid ""
"The Läsbarhetsindex (Lix) formula can be used on documents of any Western "
"European language. A <a href=\"#lix-gauge\">chart</a> is also available "
"to visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Rate Index" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1661
msgid ""
"The Rate Index (Rix) formula is a variation of Lix and can be used on "
"documents of any Western European language."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1687
msgid ""
"Coleman-Liau is meant for secondary age (4th grade to college level) "
"readers. This formula is based on text from the .4 to 16.3 grade level "
"range. This test usually yields the lowest grade when applied to "
"technical documents."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1713
msgid "Danielson-Bryan 1 is designed for student materials."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1729
msgid ""
"Danielson-Bryan 2 is designed for student materials. It is a variation of "
"Flesch Reading Ease that uses character counts instead of syllable "
"counts. A <a href=\"#danielson-bryan-2\">chart</a> is also available to "
"visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1747
msgid ""
"FORCAST was devised for assessing U.S. Army technical manuals and forms. "
"It is the only test not designed for running narrative, so it is mostly "
"appropriate for multiple-choice quizzes, applications, entrance forms, "
"etc."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Flesch Reading Ease" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1773
msgid ""
"Farr-Jenkins-Paterson is a variation of the Flesch Reading Ease test, "
"which uses the mono-syllabic word count instead of the overall syllable "
"count. Scores range from 0-100 (the higher the score, the easier to "
"read). Average documents should be within the range of 60-70."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1792
msgid ""
"A modified version of Farr-Jenkins-Paterson designed for U.S. Navy "
"technical manuals and forms."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1809
msgid ""
"PSK Farr-Jenkins-Paterson is a variation of the Farr-Jenkins-Paterson "
"test, which returns a grade score instead of a Flesch difficulty level."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Flesch Reading Ease" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1827
msgid ""
"Flesch Reading Ease is meant for secondary and adult-level text and is a "
"standard used by many U.S. government agencies, including the U.S. "
"Department of Defense. Scores range from 0-100 (the higher the score, the "
"easier to read). Average documents should be within the range of 60-70. A "
"<a href=\"#flesch-chart\">chart</a> is also available to visualize the "
"score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1865 projects/base_project.cpp:1891
msgid ""
"Flesch-Kincaid is designed for technical documents and is mostly "
"applicable to manuals and forms, rather than schoolbook text or literary "
"works.\n"
"\n"
"This test is part of the Kincaid Navy Personnel collection of tests."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "New Fog Count" should not be translated; it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1911
msgid ""
"New Fog Count is a modified version of Gunning Fog created for the U.S. "
"Navy and was designed for technical documents and manuals.\n"
"\n"
"This test is part of the Kincaid Navy Personnel collection of tests."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1932
msgid ""
"The McAlpine EFLAW formula is used to determine the ease of reading "
"English text for ESL/EFL (English as a Second/Foreign Language) readers. "
"This test is influenced by sentence length and words consisting of three "
"or less characters. To lower a score, try using shorter sentences and "
"longer, less colloquial words."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1952 projects/base_project.cpp:1984
msgid ""
"SMOG is generally appropriate for secondary age (4th grade to college "
"level) readers. SMOG tests for 100% comprehension, whereas most formulas "
"test for around 50%-75% comprehension."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1983
msgid "SMOG (simplified)"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Modified SMOG" should not be translated; it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:2004
msgid ""
"Modified SMOG is a variation of SMOG that is adjusted for primary-age "
"materials."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "New Automated Readability Index" should not be translated;
#. it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:2021 projects/base_project.cpp:2041
msgid ""
"New Automated Readability Index is a modified version of ARI created for "
"U.S. Navy materials and was designed for technical documents and "
"manuals.\n"
"\n"
"This test is part of the Kincaid Navy Personnel collection of tests."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:2061
msgid "PSK Flesch is used for student readers."
msgstr ""

